    "message": {
     "content": "### 1. Compensation Breakdown: Old vs. Final Offer vs. Meta\n\nYour negotiation was a major success. Adding a **$200,000 sign-on bonus** and matching your base salary at **$240,000** changes the math substantially.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Year-by-Year Cash Flow Comparison\n\nGoogle's new-hire grants standardly front-load equity (typically **38% Year 1, 32% Year 2, 20% Year 3, 10% Year 4** with monthly vesting). \n\n| Year | Meta (Estimated) | Google Final Offer (Front-loaded) | Google Final Offer (Even 25%/yr) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Year 1** | ~$476k\u2013$526k | **~$898,000** <br> *(Base $240k + Bonus $48k + Sign-on $200k + Equity $410k)* | **~$758,000** <br> *(Base $240k + Bonus $48k + Sign-on $200k + Equity $270k)* |\n| **Year 2** | ~$526k | **~$633,600** <br> *(+ any Y1 refresher vest)* | **~$558,000** <br> *(+ any Y1 refresher vest)* |\n| **Year 3** | ~$526k | **~$504k** + Refresher stack (~$100k+) | **~$558k** + Refresher stack |\n| **Year 4** | ~$526k | **~$396k** + Refresher stack (~$200k+) | **~$558k** + Refresher stack |\n\n### What this means:\n* **Massive Year 1 windfall:** You will take home **$230k to $370k+ more** in Year 1 than you would staying at Meta.\n* **The unvested equity at Meta is fully made whole:** The $200,000 sign-on bonus replaces the $200,000 in Meta stock you would walk away from, while your Google equity vests *on top* of it starting in month one.\n* **Top-of-market L6 package:** At roughly **~$1.28M total value over 4 years in equity + base + target bonus + sign-on**, this represents the upper quartile of Google L6 PM offers.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Should You Take It?\n\n**From a purely financial standpoint: Yes, accept.**\n\nBecause you were not looking and are happy at Meta, weigh these final points before signing:\n\n#### Reasons to Accept:\n1. **Financial outperformance:** You lock in near-$900k compensation in your first 12 months with zero downside risk to your base salary.\n2. **Career diversification:** Having both Meta (IC6) and Google (L6) Product Management on your resume opens virtually every executive/VP door across the tech industry for future roles.\n3. **Pace and sustainability:** Google PM roles often offer better work-life balance and sustainability compared to Meta's aggressive PSC/performance review cycles.\n\n#### Reasons to Consider Staying at Meta:\n1. **Velocity and culture:** Meta's product shipping cycles and engineering-to-PM autonomy are significantly faster than Google's consensus-heavy culture.\n2. **Established reputation:** If you are on an active promotion track toward IC7 / Director at Meta, moving to Google resets that timeline by at least 18\u201324 months.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Checklist Before You Sign\n\n1. **Sign-On Payment Schedule & Clawback:** Confirm if the $200k is paid in a single lump sum on your first paycheck and whether the clawback period is **12 or 24 months** (prorated).\n2. **Equity Vesting Cadence:** Verify whether your $1,080,000 grant follows the front-loaded schedule (38/32/20/10) with monthly vesting and no cliff.\n3. **Start Date Flexibility:** Ensure your start date allows you to capture any imminent Meta bonus/vesting milestone if it falls in the immediate weeks ahead.",
